  "summary_en": "U.S. Coast Guard regulation (33 CFR Part 101) setting general maritime security rules under the Maritime Transportation Security Act and SOLAS/ISPS: MARSEC levels, TWIC access control, enforcement and penalties, plus a 2025 cybersecurity subpart for IT/OT systems on U.S. vessels and facilities. No AI or robotics content.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Establishes MARSEC Levels 1-3 and Coast Guard directives for ports, vessels, facilities.",
   "Requires TWIC electronic inspection and access control for secure areas.",
   "Civil penalties up to $25,000 per violation; control and compliance measures including detention.",
   "Subpart F requires Cybersecurity Plans, Cybersecurity Officers, drills, assessments, and penetration testing.",
   "Mandates incident reporting to the National Response Center and IT/OT network segmentation."
